OL,3,GNEWSAThe bridge that brings an entire
OL,4,Atown to a halt
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpanning nearly 1,300m (4,265ft),
OL,7,Fpropped on concrete pillars and framing
OL,8,Fa view which inspired George Orwell's
OL,9,Fpen name, it has become known as the
OL,10,Fgateway to East Anglia.
OL,12,FBut when the Orwell Bridge, which
OL,13,Fcarries the A14 east to west on the
OL,14,Foutskirts of Ipswich, grinds to a halt,
OL,15,Fthat gateway slams shut, bringing
OL,16,Fgridlock to an entire town and slowing
OL,17,Fdown the rest of Suffolk.
OL,19,FIt is a problem which has plagued this
OL,20,Fkey route for Felixstowe, Britain's
OL,21,Flargest container port, for more than
OL,22,F40 years.
OL,23,APub: 17-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
